    "key": "b54325d5cfb373ea25b4f7772bfd9d648012827b",
    "name": "Checkbox",
    "type": "COMPONENT_SET",
    "description": "— s2a:meta —\nversion:    1.0.0\nstatus:     active\nupdated:    2026-08-26\nchangelog:\n  1.0.0   2026-08-04  init         Initial release\n\nA single checkbox with a label — toggles one independent option on or off.\n\n## Good to know\nUse a checkbox for a standalone yes/no choice. For picking one option from several, use Radio; for a full-width selectable row with an icon, use CheckboxTile.\nLight and dark are automatic — the box, checkmark, and label all bind s2a/color/content/default, which re-resolves from the page or surface theme mode. There is no separate dark variant.\nThe whole row is the target — clicking the label toggles the box, not just the box itself.\n\n## Accessibility\nExposes a native checkbox role with the label programmatically associated, so assistive tech announces the label and the checked/unchecked state (WCAG 2.2 AA · SC 4.1.2 Name, Role, Value; SC 1.3.1 Info & Relationships).\nKeyboard: Tab moves focus to the checkbox, Space toggles it; the focused state shows a visible focus ring (SC 2.1.1 Keyboard; SC 2.4.7 Focus Visible).\nBecause the checkmark and label use s2a/color/content/default, contrast is maintained in both light and dark themes (SC 1.4.3 Contrast Minimum).",
    "meta": {
      "version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "active",
      "updated": "2026-08-26",
      "changelog": "1.0.0   2026-08-04  init         Initial release"
